import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 706 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition | The Transcendent One's Civilizational Weight — Individual Combat Power = Destructive Power × Civilizational Consensus","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 706 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition | The Transcendent One's Civilizational Weight — Individual Combat Power = Destructive Power × Civilizational Consensus","no":706,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Civilizational Weight","Combat-Power Formula","Civilizational Consensus","Alaya Network"],"related":["29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","17-Plane-Sovereign Strong-One Standard","01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0706_模块4-超脱者的文明权重.md","filePath":"en/0706_模块4-超脱者的文明权重.md"}`),a={name:"en/0706_模块4-超脱者的文明权重.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,h,u){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-706-transcendence-orthodox-definition-the-transcendent-one-s-civilizational-weight-—-individual-combat-power-destructive-power-×-civilizational-consensus" tabindex="-1">Entry 706 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition | The Transcendent One&#39;s Civilizational Weight — Individual Combat Power = Destructive Power × Civilizational Consensus <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-706-transcendence-orthodox-definition-the-transcendent-one-s-civilizational-weight-—-individual-combat-power-destructive-power-×-civilizational-consensus" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 706 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition | The Transcendent One&#39;s Civilizational Weight — Individual Combat Power = Destructive Power × Civilizational Consensus&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 29, 17, 01</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-looking-only-at-destructive-power-is-the-old-world-s-algorithm" tabindex="-1">Introduction: looking only at destructive power is the old world&#39;s algorithm <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-looking-only-at-destructive-power-is-the-old-world-s-algorithm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: looking only at destructive power is the old world&#39;s algorithm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Web-novel systems evaluate a strong one by only one number: combat power. One fist shatters how many planets, one finger extinguishes how many galaxies; the bigger the number the stronger. This algorithm is thoroughly rewritten in Heng Yuan Zhou. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s formula is:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Individual effective combat power = destructive power × civilizational consensus</strong></p></blockquote><p>This multiplication rather than addition means that as either variable approaches zero, effective combat power approaches zero. A strong one with off-the-charts destructive power but negative civilizational consensus, in Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s ledger, is not &quot;very strong,&quot; but &quot;high-risk&quot; — the harder he works, the greater the damage to civilization.</p><p>The six top-level axioms in this entry are simultaneously mathematized: the anti-predation axiom is the premise that &quot;destructive power&quot; must have a clean source; the republican axiom of Myriad Races is the legal source of &quot;civilizational consensus&quot;; the collective-ascension axiom requires the strong one&#39;s effective combat power ultimately serve ascension, not personal bravado; the causal self-discipline axiom constrains procedure when the strong one calls on destructive power; the law-first axiom ensures this formula itself is a law-level definition, not modified by any protagonist halo.</p><p>Universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing/layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more higher-level infinity. Everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, so predation naturally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-what-is-civilizational-weight-from-destructive-power-to-effective-combat-power" tabindex="-1">I: What Is Civilizational Weight: From &quot;Destructive Power&quot; to &quot;Effective Combat Power&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-what-is-civilizational-weight-from-destructive-power-to-effective-combat-power" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I: What Is Civilizational Weight: From &quot;Destructive Power&quot; to &quot;Effective Combat Power&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>First nail the terminology. <strong>Civilizational weight</strong> is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s quantified indicator of a cultivator&#39;s actual influence in the Anchor Symbiotic Network, computed in real time by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision. It is not a moral score, not a good-person card, but a <strong>public-compute allocation voucher</strong> — the higher the weight, the greater the law network&#39;s public compute you can call, cross-plane channel quotas, and contracted-responsibility resource-pool share.</p><p>The old system only computes destructive power; Heng Yuan Zhou puts destructive power in the civilizational-weight formula as multiplication:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Definition</th><th>Range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Destructive power</td><td>The maximum disturbance this individual can cause to the law network in extreme cases</td><td>0 to +∞</td></tr><tr><td>Civilizational consensus</td><td>Myriad-Rank representatives&#39; and Alaya Network&#39;s composite score of his power&#39;s lawfulness, direction correctness, and contribution sustainability</td><td>-1 to +1</td></tr><tr><td>Effective combat power</td><td>Destructive power × civilizational consensus</td><td>May be negative</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The key is civilizational consensus may be negative. A predation-faction strong one has immense destructive power, but his existence is recognized by Myriad Ranks as &quot;harm,&quot; with consensus negative; his effective combat power on the civilization ledger is negative — that is, the stronger he is, the poorer civilization becomes because of him. This is not metaphor; this is how the Alaya Network actually keeps accounts.</p><h2 id="ii-how-civilizational-consensus-is-computed-five-sub-items" tabindex="-1">II: How Civilizational Consensus Is Computed: Five Sub-Items <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-how-civilizational-consensus-is-computed-five-sub-items" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II: How Civilizational Consensus Is Computed: Five Sub-Items&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational consensus is not voted out, but the Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision computes by five sub-items weighted:</p><ol><li><strong>Source lawfulness (weight 25%)</strong>: whether power comes from the Myriad-Rank origin two-way cycle, with no predation residual marks;</li><li><strong>Direction correctness (weight 25%)</strong>: whether his daily work serves Myriad-Rank symbiosis, whether he refuses running away, lying flat, and monopolizing;</li><li><strong>Contribution sustainability (weight 20%)</strong>: whether his post performance continuously outputs civilization increment, not one-off heroism;</li><li><strong>Coverage breadth (weight 15%)</strong>: the number of clans, planes, and life forms his work benefits;</li><li><strong>Procedural compliance (weight 15%)</strong>: whether cross-plane and cross-time operations strictly follow causal self-discipline reporting.</li></ol><p>Any sub-item going to zero directly drags consensus down; source lawfulness alone being negative makes consensus directly negative. This algorithm ensures: <strong>you cannot whitewash &quot;long-term predation&quot; by &quot;occasionally doing good,&quot; nor bypass &quot;wrong direction&quot; by &quot;invincible combat power.&quot;</strong></p><h2 id="iii-why-multiplication-not-addition" tabindex="-1">III: Why Multiplication Not Addition <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-why-multiplication-not-addition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III: Why Multiplication Not Addition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Designing it as multiplication is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s actuarial choice under the law-first axiom:</p><ul><li>If addition, a predation-faction strong one with immense destructive power, even with very low consensus, could still rank high on total score by destructive power — this is the mathematical root of the old world&#39;s &quot;might makes right&quot;;</li><li>Multiplication makes consensus the &quot;switch&quot; of destructive power: consensus negative, and however great destructive power is only a negative asset;</li><li>Multiplication also keeps &quot;right direction but small power&quot; latecomers from being buried — as long as consensus is high enough, his effective combat power linearly amplifies with power growth, and the amplification direction is civilization increment.</li></ul><p>First-generation anchors like Lin Hao, with limited early power, but with clean source, right direction, broad coverage, and procedural compliance, kept consensus above 0.9 long-term; later his destructive power grew with realm, and effective combat power soared synchronously — not because he suddenly turned fierce, but because his &quot;fierceness&quot; was from the beginning recognized by Myriad Ranks and lawfully called by the law network.</p><h2 id="iv-how-civilizational-weight-in-turn-constrains-the-transcendent-one" tabindex="-1">IV: How Civilizational Weight in Turn Constrains the Transcendent One <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-how-civilizational-weight-in-turn-constrains-the-transcendent-one" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV: How Civilizational Weight in Turn Constrains the Transcendent One&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational weight is not an award, but a <strong>rein</strong>. After the transcendent one enters the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm, his civilizational-weight panel is open to Myriad-Rank representatives:</p><ul><li>The Myriad-Rank republican council may periodically deliberate his weight composition; any sub-item declining for two consecutive cycles triggers a post talk;</li><li>Weight falling below a threshold automatically downgrades his law-anchor permissions — not punishment, but preventing a direction-drifting strong one from continuing to call public compute;</li><li>What weight rise brings is not privilege inflation, but post upgrade: you can take on larger civilizational engineering, be responsible for more planes, train more transcendent ones.</li></ul><p>This is the mathematized expression of &quot;the stronger the more he must work&quot;: <strong>civilizational weight is not a reward for working more, but a voucher for being able to lawfully keep working more.</strong> If you don&#39;t work, weight drops; weight drops, your destructive power remains but effective combat power goes to zero, equal to self-disarming.</p><h2 id="v-contrast-with-tang-luo-and-gu-chensha-systems" tabindex="-1">V: Contrast with Tang-Luo and Gu Chensha Systems <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-contrast-with-tang-luo-and-gu-chensha-systems" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V: Contrast with Tang-Luo and Gu Chensha Systems&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Module 2 has repeatedly argued that the Tang-Luo system&#39;s protagonist-uniqueness dependence rating is &quot;high,&quot; and the Gu Chensha system&#39;s is &quot;very high.&quot; From the civilizational-weight view, these two systems&#39; illness is exactly the same: <strong>the whole civilization&#39;s &quot;effective combat power&quot; is compressed into one private node.</strong> Gu Chensha&#39;s destructive power is immense, but his civilizational consensus is missing in the Myriad-Rank dimension — Myriad Ranks do not recognize him, they fear him. Under the multiplication formula, his &quot;effective combat power&quot; is actually only his personal destructive power; the whole network does not endorse him, and once he has a problem, civilization has no second node to take over.</p><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s network-style transcendence, with protagonist-uniqueness dependence &quot;very low&quot;: the Myriad-Rank origin two-way cycle shares civilizational weight across tens of millions of lawful nodes, and any one node going offline, the network runs as usual. Lin Hao is not &quot;the only protagonist&quot;; he is &quot;the first to run the civilizational-weight formula through&quot; — once he runs it through, the formula opens to all beings.</p><h2 id="vi-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VI: Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI: Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the multiplication formula directs &quot;destructive power&quot; into &quot;effective combat power,&quot; eliminating meaningless consumption of pure destructive power on civilization</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the source-lawfulness sub-item seals predators&#39; whitewash path at the algorithm level, and predation-faction strong ones&#39; consensus must be negative</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo systems&#39; combat-power algorithm is addition (big power = awesome); Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s is multiplication (power must be consensus-recognized to be awesome)</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the coverage-breadth sub-item explicitly lists Myriad-Rank clans and life forms in consensus computation, and clans the strong one does not serve drag down his weight</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the civilizational-weight formula itself is queryable in the Selfless Dao public library, and all beings can compute their own weight accounts</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: the universal equal infinite law — within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation naturally loses meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Individual combat power = destructive power × civilizational consensus. This formula is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s hardest rewrite of the word &quot;strong one.&quot; It tells all cultivators: <strong>your destructive power is your own affair; your civilizational consensus is Myriad Ranks&#39; affair; only when Myriad Ranks recognize your direction may your destructive power be called combat power.</strong> The transcendent one transcends not because his destructive power is greatest, but because his civilizational consensus is highest — so high that every bit of his destructive power is simultaneously Myriad Ranks&#39; protective power.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/17-位面至高强者标准.html">Entry 17 · Plane-Sovereign Strong-One Standard</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/01-锚点共生文明宣言.html">Entry 01 · Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">Entry 22 · Resource-Allocation Contracted-Responsibility Mechanism</a></li></ul>',34)])])}const m=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
